My DevOps Journey: Day 1 Introduction

What is DevOps?
DevOps is a set of practices that combines development and operations to shorten the systems development life cycle and provide continuous delivery with high software quality. By integrating automation, collaboration, and continuous feedback into the process, DevOps helps speed up the development pipeline and improves software reliability.

What is SecOps?
SecOps, on the other hand, integrates security practices into the DevOps pipeline, ensuring that security is never an afterthought. It focuses on automating security checks, vulnerability scanning, and risk mitigation to ensure software is secure from the start.
Together, DevOps and SecOps create a collaborative, efficient, and secure pipeline for delivering high-quality software quickly.
